# ==========================================================================
#  O76  Challenge: the day a second edition appears
# ==========================================================================
#
#  DECIDES
#    Split bs:Work into Work and Edition so that the compromise of o10 is
#    retired, every assertion made under the old meaning stays true, the
#    competency questions still answer, and the reasoner agrees; an answer
#    is beside the lesson, to be read after yours.
#
#  WHY
#    The brief that arrives after the site launches: Bell Rock has issued a
#    second edition of The Book Town, with a new ISBN and a different page
#    count, and the committee wants both stocked and told apart. Under the
#    shipped vocabulary a work has one ISBN, functionally, so there is no
#    way to say it. o10 recorded the compromise and o27 said what the fix
#    must respect: the meaning of bs:Work must not move under the data
#    already written.
#
#    The task, then. Introduce bs:Edition with an identity criterion of its
#    own, the ISBN, as a key. Decide which of bs:Work's properties are the
#    work's (author, title, genre, original language) and which are the
#    edition's (publisher, ISBN, pages, price, publication year), and move
#    only the second group, with a change note on each. Decide how existing
#    bs:Work assertions carrying an ISBN are migrated: a first edition
#    minted per work is one answer. Keep Work and Edition disjoint, since
#    their criteria of identity differ. Decide the version number by the
#    diff (o71). Then check: OWL 2 DL; consistent with the data; the stock
#    records now point at editions, and question 10 in the brief still
#    answers; and a query for 'the editions of The Book Town' returns two.
#
#    answer.ttl beside this lesson is one way to do it, measured: DL,
#    consistent, with the migration of one work shown. It is not the only
#    way. A version that keeps bs:Work for editions and mints a new
#    bs:AbstractWork above it is defensible, and the argument about which
#    is better is the argument this course was about.
#
#  DIAGRAM
#       before                                   after
#       bs:Work  isbn, pages, publishedBy,       bs:Work      author, title, genre, originalLanguage
#                author, title, genre            bs:Edition   editionOf (functional), isbn (key), pages, publishedBy, rrp, publicationYear
#                                                Work and Edition disjoint: different criteria of identity
#
#       acceptance
#       - OWL 2 DL; consistent with the data
#       - every 2.x assertion still true of something (the work, or its first edition)
#       - question 10 still answers; 'editions of The Book Town' returns two
#       - version-diff says MAJOR, and the change notes say why
#
#  WHAT TO TAKE AWAY
#    - The day the identity criterion changes is the day a class splits.
#      The split is a new term, not a new meaning for the old one.
#    - Sort the properties by which referent they belong to. The design
#      work is that sorting; the axioms follow.
#    - Acceptance is measured: profile, reasoner, competency questions,
#      diff. Read the answer only after yours passes them.
#
#  NOTE
#    The checker measures answer.ttl as well: python
#    scripts/check_lessons.py o76 --show prints what HermiT and the profile
#    checker made of it. To measure your own, put it in place of answer.ttl
#    and run the same command.
#
#  CORNER    all three
#  RUNS IN   the browser
#  OPEN IN THE EDITOR
#            https://semantechs.co.uk/turtle-editor-viewer/?dot=https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fpwin%2FOntology_Course%2Fmain%2Flessons%2F12-putting-it-together%2Fo76-challenge-the-day-a-second-edition-appears.ttl
#  SOURCES   OBO Foundry principle FP-019, stability of term meaning
#            https://obofoundry.org/principles/fp-019-term-stability.html
#            SemOps Manual 12.1 Evidence-based semver: version-diff
#            https://github.com/pwin/SemOpsManual/blob/main/docs/12-release-and-change.md#121-evidence-based-semver-version-diff
#  MEASURED  parses, 6 triples; OWL 2 DL in profile; answer.ttl: OWL 2 DL, consistent
# ==========================================================================

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

skos:prefLabel      a owl:AnnotationProperty .
skos:definition     a owl:AnnotationProperty .
skos:editorialNote  a owl:AnnotationProperty .

<https://example.org/bookshop-trail/schema>
    a                   owl:Ontology ;
    skos:prefLabel      "The Bookshop Trail schema, 3.0.0 (the challenge)"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote  "Your answer goes here. answer.ttl beside this lesson is one answer, measured."@en .
